Why?
Security best practice:
Never use root/postgres user in applications.

 9️⃣ Basic SQL Operations (CRUD)

CRUD = Create, Read, Update, Delete

Create Table
CREATE TABLE students (
    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100),
    email VARCHAR(100)
);




Insert Data
INSERT INTO students (name, email)
VALUES ('Mohit', 'mohit@gmail.com');



Read Data
SELECT * FROM students;
Update Data
UPDATE students
SET name = 'Mohit'
WHERE id = 1;
Delete Data
DELETE FROM students WHERE id = 1;



 1️⃣0️⃣ What is ACID? (Very Important Concept)

PostgreSQL follows ACID properties.

A — Atomicity

Transaction either fully completes or fails completely.

C — Consistency

Database remains valid before and after transaction.

I — Isolation

Transactions do not interfere with each other.

D — Durability

Once committed, data is permanently saved.

Example:
Bank transfer system.



 1️⃣1️⃣ What is Index?
Definition:

An index improves search performance.

Without index:
Full table scan.

With index:
Faster lookup.

Example:

CREATE INDEX idx_email ON students(email);






